  "units": "cm",
  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for spherical mirrors and their focus, book pages 223–228 and 235, topics 8.4, 8.5, 8.6 and 8.8.3, next to চিত্র ৮.১৭, ৮.১৮, ৮.২১ and ৮.২৭. A piece is cut from a hollow glass sphere of radius r, silvered on its inner surface and stood on an optical bench with a printed cm scale: parallel light from a ray box meets at the focus F, and f reads r/2 on the scale for every r the student chooses, while a wide bundle shows why that is only nearly true. A half turn and a coat on the other surface make a convex mirror: the light spreads, and only seems to come from F behind it. A bulb at the concave mirror's F gives a parallel beam, as in a torch; the student can move it off F. All rays are traced on the exact sphere. Five test questions on the picture. Offline, Bangla and English.",
